(Nick @ The End of Time) writes:
> The linker cannot satisfy the references to the following routines:-
> 
> _FD_ZERO
> _FD_SET
> _FD_ISSET
> 
> These are all called from inside interface.c.

  There are macros for manipulating the bit masks used by the select()
system call.  You can probably add the following macro definitions to
the top of interface.c to make up for the fact that they are missing:

  #define FD_ZERO(p)  ((p)->fds_bits[0] = 0)
  #define FD_SET(n, p)   ((p)->fds_bits[0] |= (1 << (n)))
  #define FD_ISSET(n, p)   ((p)->fds_bits[0] & (1 << (n)))

If those don't work, try these:

  #define FD_ZERO(p)  ((p) = 0)
  #define FD_SET(n, p)   ((p) |= (1 << (n)))
  #define FD_ISSET(n, p)   ((p) & (1 << (n)))

